## Basic Usage

### Importing Components

Ant Design components can be imported individually to optimize bundle size:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Button, DatePicker, message } from 'antd';
import 'antd/dist/reset.css';

const App = () => {
  const handleClick = () => {
    message.success('Button clicked!');
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ padding: '20px' }}>
      <Button type="primary" onClick={handleClick}>
        Primary Button
      </Button>
      <DatePicker style={{ marginLeft: '10px' }} />
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
```

### Using Icons

Ant Design provides a comprehensive icon library:

```jsx
import { SearchOutlined, UserOutlined, SettingOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

const IconExample = () => (
  <div>
    <SearchOutlined style={{ fontSize: '24px', color: '#1890ff' }} />
    <UserOutlined style={{ fontSize: '24px', marginLeft: '10px' }} />
    <SettingOutlined style={{ fontSize: '24px', marginLeft: '10px' }} />
  </div>
);
```

## Core Components Overview

### Layout Components

Ant Design provides flexible layout components:

- **Layout**: Basic layout container
- **Grid**: 24-column grid system
- **Space**: Component spacing
- **Divider**: Content divider

### Navigation Components

- **Menu**: Navigation menu
- **Breadcrumb**: Breadcrumb navigation
- **Pagination**: Page navigation
- **Steps**: Step-by-step process

### Data Entry Components

- **Form**: Form with validation
- **Input**: Text input fields
- **Select**: Dropdown selection
- **DatePicker**: Date selection
- **Upload**: File upload

### Data Display Components

- **Table**: Data table
- **Card**: Content container
- **List**: List display
- **Descriptions**: Key-value pairs

## Practical Examples

### Creating a Simple Form

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Form, Input, Button, Select, message } from 'antd';

const { Option } = Select;

const SimpleForm = () => {
  const [form] = Form.useForm();

  const onFinish = (values) => {
    console.log('Form values:', values);
    message.success('Form submitted successfully!');
  };

  return (
    <Form
      form={form}
      layout="vertical"
      onFinish={onFinish}
      style={{ maxWidth: '400px' }}
    >
      <Form.Item
        label="Name"
        name="name"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please input your name!' }]}
      >
        <Input placeholder="Enter your name" />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Email"
        name="email"
        rules={[
          { required: true, message: 'Please input your email!' },
          { type: 'email', message: 'Please enter a valid email!' }
        ]}
      >
        <Input placeholder="Enter your email" />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Role"
        name="role"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please select a role!' }]}
      >
        <Select placeholder="Select your role">
          <Option value="developer">Developer</Option>
          <Option value="designer">Designer</Option>
          <Option value="manager">Manager</Option>
        </Select>
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item>
        <Button type="primary" htmlType="submit">
          Submit
        </Button>
      </Form.Item>
    </Form>
  );
};

export default SimpleForm;
```

### Creating a Data Table

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Table, Tag, Space } from 'antd';

const dataSource = [
  {
    key: '1',
    name: 'John Brown',
    age: 32,
    address: 'New York No. 1 Lake Park',
    tags: ['developer', 'designer'],
  },
  {
    key: '2',
    name: 'Jim Green',
    age: 42,
    address: 'London No. 1 Lake Park',
    tags: ['manager'],
  },
];

const columns = [
  {
    title: 'Name',
    dataIndex: 'name',
    key: 'name',
  },
  {
    title: 'Age',
    dataIndex: 'age',
    key: 'age',
  },
  {
    title: 'Address',
    dataIndex: 'address',
    key: 'address',
  },
  {
    title: 'Tags',
    dataIndex: 'tags',
    key: 'tags',
    render: (tags) => (
      <>
        {tags.map((tag) => {
          let color = tag.length > 5 ? 'geekblue' : 'green';
          return (
            <Tag color={color} key={tag}>
              {tag.toUpperCase()}
            </Tag>
          );
        })}
      </>
    ),
  },
  {
    title: 'Action',
    key: 'action',
    render: (_, record) => (
      <Space size="middle">
        <a>Edit</a>
        <a>Delete</a>
      </Space>
    ),
  },
];

const DataTable = () => <Table dataSource={dataSource} columns={columns} />;

export default DataTable;
```

## Advanced Features

### Customizing Themes

Ant Design supports theme customization through CSS variables or ConfigProvider:

```jsx
import { ConfigProvider } from 'antd';

// Custom theme configuration
const theme = {
  token: {
    colorPrimary: '#00b96b',
    borderRadius: 6,
    colorBgContainer: '#f6ffed',
  },
};

const App = () => (
  <ConfigProvider theme={theme}>
    <YourAppContent />
  </ConfigProvider>
);
```

### Internationalization (i18n)

Ant Design supports multiple languages:

```jsx
import { ConfigProvider } from 'antd';
import zhCN from 'antd/locale/zh_CN';
import enUS from 'antd/locale/en_US';

// For Chinese interface
const App = () => (
  <ConfigProvider locale={zhCN}>
    <YourAppContent />
  </ConfigProvider>
);
```

### Responsive Design

Use Ant Design's responsive utilities:

```jsx
import { Grid } from 'antd';

const { useBreakpoint } = Grid;

const ResponsiveComponent = () => {
  const screens = useBreakpoint();

  return (
    <div>
      {screens.xs && <div>Mobile view</div>}
      {screens.md && <div>Tablet view</div>}
      {screens.lg && <div>Desktop view</div>}
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Import Components Selectively

```jsx
// Good - Import only what you need
import { Button, Input } from 'antd';

// Avoid - This imports everything
import * as antd from 'antd';
```

### 2. Use Proper Form Validation

```jsx
const validationRules = [
  { required: true, message: 'This field is required' },
  { min: 6, message: 'Minimum 6 characters' },
  { pattern: /^[A-Za-z]+$/, message: 'Letters only' }
];
```

### 3. Handle Loading States

```jsx
import { Spin } from 'antd';

const LoadingComponent = ({ loading, children }) => (
  <Spin spinning={loading}>
    {children}
  </Spin>
);
```

