      "description": "<p>Software stocks, like ZoomInfo (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GTM\">GTM</a>), DocuSign (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DOCU\">DOCU</a>), and HubSpot (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/HUBS\">HUBS</a>), are under pressure as the market reevaluates the sector's place in tech amid the artificial intelligence (AI) era, while OpenAI (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/OPAI.PVT\">OPAI.PVT</a>) strikes deals with Nvidia (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NVDA\">NVDA</a>) and <a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/amd-openai-sign-multibillion-dollar-132642538.html\">AMD</a> (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AMD\">AMD</a>).</p>\n<p>ZoomInfo CEO Henry Schuck joins Opening Bid with Yahoo Finance Executive Editor <a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brian-sozzi/\">Brian Sozzi </a>to discuss software companies' role in enterprises adopting AI.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:9;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
